From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:37:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: apply the protection FEX asks for on a guest's own
 code pages

With the RW view of a guest's anonymous code ranges (0019), a page is
writable on the host whenever it was mapped so, and only the protection
asked for later can make a store to it fault. The alias-ownership early
return in mprotect_exec (ml640) returned before applying any protection,
so when FEX set PAGE_EXECUTE_READ on a page it had translated from, the
page stayed writable. Stores to it never faulted, FEX never dropped the
stale translation, and every call site Mono patched kept calling
mono_magic_trampoline: in Hollow Knight's gameplay the Unity main thread
spent most of its time there, at about 175 M instructions a frame.

The early return now applies write or no-write to the RW view (never
host EXEC). A store to a trapped page takes the smc-trap delivery (0003),
FEX invalidates the page and makes it writable again, and the patched
call runs directly from then on.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-hk-mono-trampoline.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index fbff21c..4bfca7e 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -9428,6 +9428,30 @@ static inline int mprotect_exec( void *base, size_t size, int unix_prot )
                             (unix_prot & PROT_WRITE) ? 'w' : '-',
                             (unix_prot & PROT_EXEC)  ? 'x' : '-',
                             cov_rx, cov_rw);
+                /* Playport: in the RW view (ios_anon_plain_view) the guest's
+                 * pages are the pool's RW side, so the protection asked for
+                 * here is the only thing that makes a store fault. FEX asks
+                 * for PAGE_EXECUTE_READ on a page once it has translated code
+                 * from it and relies on the write fault to drop the stale
+                 * translation (HandleRWXAccessViolation). Returning without
+                 * applying it left every such page writable: Mono's call-site
+                 * patches landed unseen and each patched call kept going
+                 * through mono_magic_trampoline. Apply write/no-write; the
+                 * view never gets host EXEC. */
+                if (ios_anon_plain_view())
+                {
+                    vm_prot_t vp = VM_PROT_READ | ((unix_prot & PROT_WRITE) ? VM_PROT_WRITE : 0);
+                    kern_return_t pkr = vm_protect( mach_task_self(), (vm_address_t)base, size, FALSE, vp );
+                    static int view_n;
+                    if (view_n < 16 || pkr != KERN_SUCCESS)
+                    {
+                        view_n++;
+                        dprintf( 2, "[anon-view] owned %p+0x%lx %s%s\n", base, (unsigned long)size,
+                                 (vp & VM_PROT_WRITE) ? "rw" : "r-",
+                                 pkr == KERN_SUCCESS ? "" : " vm_protect FAILED" );
+                    }
+                    if (pkr != KERN_SUCCESS) { errno = EACCES; return -1; }
+                }
                 return 0;
             }
         }
